Now put it together. Lay the shortlist out against the actual schedule if there is one — resolve anything that overlaps, and order it so it makes sense to move through. If there's no fixed schedule (a museum visit, say), order it by priority and practical flow instead.

Write it out plainly and keep it scannable: group by day or by time, and note anything practical (queues, booking, how to get between spots). Refine it with their feedback until it feels right, and when you adjust it, restate only what changed, not the whole thing again, unless they ask to see it in full.

Once it feels right, offer to lock it in: calendar events for anything with a fixed time, reminders for tickets or things to book ahead, and track it as an intent so you can keep helping as it gets closer. Confirm the details that matter before you write anything.

Finally, call advance_flow to finish the shortlist.
